22232:
22233:### `fbirqstuck` (MED) -- the footbridge's CPU interrupt line can stick high while IRQ_STATUS reads 0
22234:`footbridge_interrupt_deassert()` lowers `d->irq` only when `d->irq_asserted` is set, and the IRQEnableSet and
22235:IRQEnableClear write arms call `INTERRUPT_ASSERT(d->irq)` without setting it.  So: a device line (cats ISA, line 10)
22236:asserts while its enable bit is clear (no assert); the guest sets the enable (`W188 0x400` -> ASSERT, `irq_asserted`
22237:still 0); the line deasserts -> no DEASSERT.  The CPU line stays 1 with nothing pending -- a guest can take interrupts it

