2387:> ### *** THE DE-ESCALATION CLAUSE �?" the one genuinely new rule, and it names a hazard this
2388:> project created for itself four times. ***
2389:>
2390:> **A fatal�+'survive fix DELETES THE ACCIDENTAL TRIPWIRE that made guard-mask growth
2391:> self-announcing.** Before #447, adding `| TCR_UNIE` to a guard mask meant `exit(1)` on the
2392:> first legal write �?" unmissable. After it, the same edit means a **silently refused write** and
2393:> nothing anywhere notices.
2394:>
2395:> So: **when a fix removes a host-fatal guard, enumerate from the diff every predicate that used
2396:> to gate death, and the detector shipping with that fix must pin the ACCEPT SIDE of each** �?" a
2397:> row per adjacent modelled bit or value, proving legal writes still land. Those rows are part
2398:> of the FIX'S COST, not future strengthening, because the fix itself destroyed the old
2399:> (accidental) detector for that class.
2400:
2401:It is bounded (the class is exactly "edits the old `exit(1)` would have announced"), and it is
2402:checkable at review time by one question: **does this diff delete `exit(` from a device? then
2403:look for accept rows.** Deliberately NOT mechanised �?" the enumeration needs judgement about
2404:adjacency, and the existing "what is the smallest edit that breaks this and still passes?" seat
2405:invocation already FINDS the instances. What was missing was never detection; it was
2406:DISPOSITION.
2407:
2408:> ### *** ACCEPT-ROW FAILABILITY �?" the companion rule, adopted 2026-08-21 after #449's accept
2409:> row was MEASURED VACUOUS. ***
2410:>
2411:> An accept-side row is **not discharged by existing** �?" it is discharged by a **MEASURED
2412:> KILL**. For each predicate the clause enumerates from the diff, build the smallest
2413:> **realistic JOINT** guard-growth mutant �?" widen the predicate **and** its diagnostic/latch
2414:> operand together, the way adjacent code actually evolves �?" and the accept row must REDDEN
2415:> under it. A row green under its own growth mutant is vacuous whatever the chosen bit's
2416:> legality.
2417:>
2418:> Choose the pinning value so a guest store can leave it **in the predicate's OPERAND**: read
2419:> the store arm, and cite its line in the row's comment. **Write-1-to-keep, write-to-clear,
2420:> read-only and never-set-by-device bits cannot carry an accept row.**
2421:
2422:**"Reaches the predicate's operand" is the checkable notion, and "the guest can produce it" is
2423:one level too shallow** �?" #449's guest *did* write CMF=1 at the interface; the store arm filtered
2424:it before the predicate ever saw it. The measured kill subsumes reachability, and it catches
2425:wrong-regex, wrong-register and wrong-width vacuities in the same row for free.
2426:
2427:*** "JOINT" WAS THE FIRST MEASURED INSTANCE OF THE RULE, NOT THE RULE �?" restated 2026-08-22
2428:by the flagship seat after #452 measured the opposite case. *** #449's guard-only widening was
