1306:## THE VACUITY FLOOR AND THE DE-ESCALATION CLAUSE (flagship adjudication, 2026-08-21)
1307:
1308:**"Weak earns its own round; vacuous does not get to ship" IS A RATIONALISATION UNTIL A FLOOR IS
1309:ATTACHED** �?" the adjudicating seat said so about the main loop's own call, and it was right:
1310:*weak* has no lower bound, so any detector that kills one mutant can claim it.
1311:
1312:> **THE FLOOR.** A detector is VACUOUS �?" replace it IN-ROUND �?" unless it (a) fails on the
1313:> pre-fix build, (b) fails on a **VERBATIM REINSTATEMENT of the removed defect at EVERY fixed
1314:> site**, and (c) fails on a **NULL MEDIUM** -- a product medium carrying none of the behaviour under
1315:> test (the clause-(c) block below says what that is per instrument kind). Below the floor, the
1316:> round's own claim to have "shipped a detector with the fix" is a WRONG RECORD, which the
1317:> stopping rule already fixes in-round.
1318:>
1319:> ### *** CLAUSE (c) -- WHAT A NULL MEDIUM IS, AND THE TWO WAYS TO RECORD IT.  Ruled 2026-10-09 by the
1320:> ### flagship seat (Fable 5.1, queue 7n-1 / 7n-2), confirmed by GPT-6 Astra with corrections, written
1321:> ### here by owner ruling.  The gloss it replaces -- "a stale copy, a comment-only file -- i.e. it
1322:> ### carries identity rows" -- is deleted, not demoted. ***
1323:>
1324:> **ONE criterion -- a product medium carrying none of the behaviour under test -- and its object
1325:> differs by instrument kind:**
1326:> * an offline differential that `#include`s the product: a COMMENT-ONLY product source, which must
1327:>   fail to COMPILE, with a gate that reds on the compile failure (measured for `#488`:
1328:>   `regress/artifacts/shortread/nullmedium_20261009/RECEIPT.txt`);
1329:> * a runtime probe: an ABSENT or NON-EMULATOR binary (every session dies), or a build WITHOUT the
1330:>   device for a device round;
1331:> * an instruction-handler round: an IDENTITY BODY (decode and retire, write nothing) -- the
1332:>   recommended default, two measured legs at `#527`.
1333:>
1334:> **THE PRE-FIX BUILD IS CLAUSE (a)'S MEDIUM AND NEVER CLAUSE (c)'S.**  It carries every behaviour of the
1335:> product, one of them wrong, so a detector can red on it and still pass a comment-only file -- `#446`,
1336:> the instance that created this clause.  A table that wrote "null medium" over a pre-fix leg carries a
1337:> WRONG RECORD (L4: correct it in place, quoting what it refutes, as
1338:> `ppcrldimimask/killtable_20260911/SCORES.txt` does), NOT a floor breach: clause (c) is then
1339:> UNMEASURED there.  **A breach is a genuine null medium coming back GREEN, and nothing else** -- "a
1340:> sharper medium was available" is not a floor criterion (at most clause-(e) debt).
1341:>
1342:> **RECORD CLAUSE (c) IN ONE OF EXACTLY TWO FORMS, never as a bare clause letter beside a row name:**
1343:> * `(c): measured at <artifact>` -- the leg was run and its receipt is durable;
1344:> * `(c): by construction via <row/pin>, leg not run` -- e.g. the gate pins the row count by EQUALITY
1345:>   and a named row reds on a dead run, or the differential `#include`s the product and its gate reds
1346:>   on a compile failure.  **A by-construction claim is checked by READING that shape; where the reading
1347:>   fails -- no runtime gate wiring, no pin, `check_min`, a control computed over the row list
1348:>   (`all([])` is True) -- the leg is OWED** (7n-1's two: the unwired `ppc_rldicl_probe.py` and
1349:>   `alpha_tbi_probe.py`).  Predict a dead run's score from the source, not from the row count (Astra
1350:>   measured luna's at 0/14 with four gate checks red, and SGI's at 6/46 because six rows test only
1351:>   exit status).
1352:>
1353:> **A claimed-but-unmeasured floor clause is L4 exactly when the record asserts a MEASUREMENT or a
1354:> NUMBER that was not made** (`#488`'s "pinned at 90": no preserved 90-row output exists, and the
1355:> differential pins 98).  The E1 `[IDENTITY]` self-count row is detector hygiene, NOT clause (c).
1356:>
1357:> ### *** CLAUSE (d) �?" NULL-REPAIR RED. Adopted 2026-08-23 by OWNER RULING, on the round
1358:> that measured its case. ***
1359:>
1360:> **(d) The detector must also fail when the fix is PRESENT but its REPAIR IS NULLED �?"
1361:> the guard kept, its effect removed.**
1362:>
1363:> **(b) DOES NOT IMPLY (d), and #461 measured both in the same hour on the same detector:**
1364:>
1365:> | mutant | shape | score |
1366:> |---|---|---|
1367:> | `m_dmarevert` | (b): reinstate the `exit(1)` verbatim | **22/31 �?" killed** |
1368:> | `m_align1` | (d): keep the guard, weaken `& 3` to `& 1` | **27/27 �?" ESCAPED** |
1369:>
1370:> The detector passed (a), (b) and (c) and was still blind to a ONE-CHARACTER edit that
1371:> re-opened the very defect the round had just closed. (b) restores the DEFECT; (d) neuters
1372:> the FIX. A detector can be sensitive to one and blind to the other, because they fail at
1373:> different sites: (b) fails where the old code was, (d) fails where the new code is.
1374:>
